  "notes": "B.S.N. Nursing (traditional undergraduate program), School of Nursing, College of Health and Human Sciences. Built from the official University of Akron Undergraduate Bulletin 'Recommended Sequence' (https://bulletin.uakron.edu/undergraduate/colleges-programs/health-professions/nursing/nursing-bs/). Per the catalog footnote, credit hours for NURS 380 Mental Health Nursing and NURS 401 RN Transition change to 4 and 3 credits respectively for students starting nursing core courses in fall 2025 or after — modeled here at the updated 4/3 credits. STAT 250 modeled at 3 credits (STAT 260 option is 3-4); total 121. Admission: 2.75 prerequisite GPA and 2.75 prerequisite science GPA, grade of C or higher in all preadmission courses, all prerequisites complete by end of spring before admission; priority/secondary admission pools apply. Junior-level clinical courses (NURS 350, 360, 370, 380) may be taken in any order (catalog footnote). Senior practicum may be NURS 450 or NURS 451 + NURS 499. Uses Akron's new course numbering.",
